From 6d7e79d09dc041fdbabe15eca60b154f15f83c46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 13:25:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [DOSKUTSU] patch 0316 -- whole-tile opaque dispatch to an
 unrolled dword copy

Round N measured the tilemap colorkey loop at 84.1% opaque pixels, and the
two tile layers move 1.01 screenfuls in ~15.9 ms = 4.9 MB/s against a
measured 17.0 MB/s memcpy floor. The per-pixel colorkey compare separates
those tiers. A tile containing no colorkey pixel does not need the compare.

Differs from patch 0145 (measured +0.40): 0145 walks a per-row run list and
pays rep-setup cost per run even on a fully opaque tile. This decides once
per tile from one bit, then runs straight-line.

No stale-tile class: tile opacity is a property of tile CONTENT. Camera
motion cannot change it and a destructible tile changes the tile INDEX, not
the pixels behind an index. Only a tilesheet reload invalidates, which frees
the table via Surface::cleanup().

Deliberately NOT named OPAQUE_TILE_FASTPATH -- that literal is in the smoke
gate at severity forbidden. The wave-38 lever of that name was never judged
on merit; it went out in a batch rollback of a 3-lever stack that regressed
14 fps on a build missing patches, with a different lever identified as the
cause. Mechanism unmeasured, not refuted; only the name is retired.

Default-OFF behind strict SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_TILE_DWORD_COPY=1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
